Package: cpxy-tsgw
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: cpxy-ng <https://github.com/simophin/cpxy-ng>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/simophin/cpxy-ng
Description: Tailscale exit node that sends its clients' traffic through a cpxy server
 A single program that joins a tailnet as an exit node, in user space: it needs no tailscaled,
 no TUN device, no routing changes and no root. Clients' TCP goes through a cpxy server, with
 local-region traffic going direct, and their DNS is answered with split DNS. Configure
 /etc/cpxy/cpxy-tsgw.conf, enable cpxy-tsgw, then log in with the link in its log.
